, exactly \\(k\\) of them are sunny, and the covering\ncondition holds. Hence a configuration exists for every integer \\(k\\) with\n\\(0\\le k\\le n\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Impossibility of larger \\(k\\)\n\nBecause the family consists of precisely \\(n\\) lines, it is impossible to have\nmore than \\(n\\) sunny lines. Therefore no \\(k>n\\) can be realized.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Conclusion\n\nThe admissible values of \\(k\\) are exactly the integers satisfying  \n\n\\[\n0\\le k\\le n .\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{All integers }k\\text{ with }0\\le k\\le n\\text{ are possible.}}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
