n \\(\\mathcal L_{k}\\) shows that every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) is attainable.  \n   Hence the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-2\\}} .\n   \\]"
